# Linux packaging keeps LF: shell scripts, and the udev rule the Rust test compares byte for byte.
src-tauri/linux/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
.github/** text eol=lf
# Frame fixtures and generated tables that tests compare byte for byte with what the code writes: LF in every checkout,
# so a fresh Windows clone (core.autocrlf=true) passes npm test too.
*-frames.txt text eol=lf
*-cases.txt text eol=lf
*.generated.ts text eol=lf
# Vendored upstream sources stay byte-identical to upstream.
scripts/controllers/sdl/** text eol=lf
# Kept in the development repo, left out of the published source (git archive): design-review screenshots and the
# brief the logo was commissioned with.
release/*-shots/** export-ignore
# The head-to-head Sandbox configs name this PC's folders (their host paths): kept here, not published.
release/sandbox-test/compare/*.wsb export-ignore
branding/BRIEF.md export-ignore
